  "description": {
    "ja": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 日本語版「ギンバイカ」",
      "source_url": "https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E3%82%AE%E3%83%B3%E3%83%90%E3%82%A4%E3%82%AB",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 108335657,
      "text": "ギンバイカ は、フトモモ科の単型の属ギンバイカ属の常緑低木。地中海沿岸原産。イタリア語でミルト。英語でマートル。ドイツ語ではミュルテ（Myrte）。属名からミルトス とも呼ぶ。花が結婚式などの飾りによく使われるので「祝いの木」ともいう。"
    },
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 英語版「Myrtus communis」",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Myrtus_communis",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 1369952906,
      "text": "Myrtus communis, the common myrtle or true myrtle, is an Old World species of flowering plant in the myrtle family, Myrtaceae. It forms an evergreen shrub."
    }
  },
  "sections": {
    "cultivation": {
      "en": {
        "source": "Wikipedia 英語版「Myrtus communis」の節「Cultivation」",
        "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Myrtus_communis#Cultivation",
        "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
        "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
        "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
        "revision": 1369952906,
        "heading": "Cultivation",
        "text": "This species and the more compact M. communis subsp. tarentina have won the Royal Horticultural Society's Award of Garden Merit. They are hardy but prefer a sheltered position in full sun.\nThe plant can be propagated with seeds stratified for 3 months. Also, one can use a cutting with a short heel (small part of the bark), keeping it in moistened rooting mix.",
        "truncated": false
      }
    }
